{:edb/db-before-t 1054 :edb/db-after-t 1055 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534367 50 #inst "2026-10-06T17:22:37.789Z" 13194139534367 true] [17592186114973 1100 "Find $AB-CB$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534367 false] [17592186114973 1100 "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186114973 1145 "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA - C &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&=-I_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB - CB &= (A - C)B \\\\\n&=-I_{3}B \\\\\n&=-B \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534367 false] [17592186114973 1145 "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186114974 1100 "Calculate $ABC$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534367 false] [17592186114974 1100 "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186114974 1145 "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC)\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore,\n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBC &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nABC &= A(BC) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534367 false] [17592186114974 1145 "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186114975 1100 "Given that $A, B$, and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n1. $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n2. $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n3. $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" 13194139534367 false] [17592186114975 1100 "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\n- $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\n- $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186114975 1145 "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." 13194139534367 true] [17592186114975 1145 "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n$AB + AC \\neq BA + CA$.\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC$, and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." 13194139534367 false] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284281 13194139534367 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284309 13194139534367 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284317 13194139534367 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284324 13194139534367 true] [17592186115146 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284376 13194139534367 true] [17592186115147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284334 13194139534367 true] [17592186115147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284341 13194139534367 true] [17592186115147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284348 13194139534367 true] [17592186115147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284355 13194139534367 true] [17592186115147 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284362 13194139534367 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284288 13194139534367 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284295 13194139534367 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284302 13194139534367 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284369 13194139534367 true] [17592186115148 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284383 13194139534367 true] [17592186284281 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284282 13194139534367 true] [17592186284281 1089 "q-130269" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284281 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534367 true] [17592186284281 1100 "Calculate $BA+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284281 1113 #uuid "d1b62d90-2496-5af6-bac3-452acf9abda8" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284281 1145 "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nBA+BC=B(A+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA+BC & =B(A+C) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284283 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284284 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284285 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284286 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284287 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1041 "selection" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284283 13194139534367 true] [17592186284282 1110 #uuid "f5def946-074f-51ba-aec2-408a7d0b5170" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284283 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534367 true] [17592186284283 1111 #uuid "9b8ca444-6c66-54ed-845f-78a70554ec28" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284284 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534367 true] [17592186284284 1111 #uuid "0818345a-ed06-5552-ba9c-5204a8c6abfb" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284285 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534367 true] [17592186284285 1111 #uuid "f5f8e967-74b3-57af-bf45-28e2793f20e9" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284286 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534367 true] [17592186284286 1111 #uuid "67c014cb-d190-5071-83f1-5c2a13627f0b" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284287 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534367 true] [17592186284287 1111 #uuid "cc0793b8-872b-5d21-8f1c-c8c8f7cb3f34" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284288 1017 #edb/ref 17592186284289 13194139534367 true] [17592186284288 1089 "q-130449" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284288 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534367 true] [17592186284288 1100 "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $3\\times 3$ matrices, and  ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=A{I}_{3}B$\n- $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$\n- ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284288 1113 #uuid "0e3975d8-0204-5147-a2bf-df4657a2f13f" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284288 1145 "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $A{I}_{3}B=(A{I}_{3})B=AB.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB+A{I}_{3}=AB+A.$ However,  $AB+A\\ne AB,$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284290 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284291 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284292 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284293 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1000 #edb/ref 17592186284294 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1041 "selection" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1104 #edb/ref 17592186284290 13194139534367 true] [17592186284289 1110 #uuid "4d147b5f-6d58-5c16-b472-c51cdf38be30" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284290 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534367 true] [17592186284290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534367 true] [17592186284290 1111 #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" 1319